{"claim": "The peer.reboot dashboard tile draws a fixed 150x150 canvas but its status line (.rebootstatus) sits in normal flow BELOW the canvas, so a long message grows the tile and pushes the rows below it down instead of painting over a neighbour.", "detail": "R2.7 (2026-11-05). The icon slot in peer.headsup css (D4) is min-height:150px, not a fixed height, so the tile grows with its status. peer.reboot's redraw() sizes the canvas square from the slot WIDTH (h = w), never clientHeight, so the drawing stays 150x150 however tall the status gets. The status is textContent-only, one div per line. Verified in the rig at 1440x900, panel 360px, and with the tiles reordered Reboot->Camera: the ~374-char Linux failure sentence grew the reboot tile to 412px and the camera tile moved down a clean 12px gap with no overlap.", "tags": "peer,reboot,ui,dashboard,layout,R2.7", "source": {"lib": "peer", "ctl": "reboot", "facet": "css", "hash": "f9d4f8149276162a"}, "confidence": "high", "time": 1793907057123},
{"end": true}]
